-- title:
--   Freeness of 𝒪[[X₁,…,Xᵣ]] over itself along Xᵢ ↦ fᵢ
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain and is adically complete for its maximal ideal, let $r$ be a natural number, and write $B = \mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_r]]$ for the ring `MvPowerSeries (Fin r) 𝒪` of formal power series in $r$ variables. Let $f : \mathrm{Fin}\,r \to B$ be an $r$-tuple of power series such that the quotient $B/(f_0,\dots,f_{r-1})$ by the ideal generated by the range of $f$ is, as an $\mathcal O$-module, both module-finite and free. Let $\varphi : B \to B$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra endomorphism with $\varphi(X_i) = f_i$ for every $i$. Then there exist a natural number $e$ and elements $\beta_0,\dots,\beta_{e-1} \in B$ such that: every $x \in B$ can be written as $x = \sum_j \varphi(c_j)\,\beta_j$ for some tuple $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,e \to B$; and whenever a tuple $c$ satisfies $\sum_j \varphi(c_j)\,\beta_j = 0$, all $c_j$ vanish. Thus the $\beta_j$ form a basis of $B$ as a module over $B$ acting through $\varphi$, the conclusion being stated in coordinates rather than as a `Module.Free` instance, and no value is asserted for the rank $e$.
--
--   This is the algebraic core of Diamond's "complete intersection implies freeness over the power series ring" step in the Taylor–Wiles patching argument: a presentation of a ring as $\mathcal O[[X]]/(f_1,\dots,f_r)$ which is finite free over $\mathcal O$ forces $\mathcal O[[X]]$ to be finite free over the subring $\mathcal O[[S]]$ acting by $S_i \mapsto f_i$. It is used by [`Algebra.PatchingDatum.nonempty_of_exists_presentation_of_free`](thm.html#Algebra.PatchingDatum.nonempty_of_exists_presentation_of_free) to produce a patching datum from such a presentation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_exists_coords_of_quotient_span_finite_free.lean

import Definitions.Def_Algebra_PatchingDatum
import Mathlib.RingTheory.DiscreteValuationRing.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.Basic
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FreeModule.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Finiteness.Defs

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

universe u

theorem MvPowerSeries.exists_coords_of_quotient_span_finite_free
    {𝒪 : Type u} [CommRing 𝒪] [IsDomain 𝒪] [IsDiscreteValuationRing 𝒪]
    [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪) 𝒪]
    {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → MvPowerSeries (Fin r) 𝒪)
    [Module.Finite 𝒪 (MvPowerSeries (Fin r) 𝒪 ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f))]
    [Module.Free 𝒪 (MvPowerSeries (Fin r) 𝒪 ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f))]
    (φ : MvPowerSeries (Fin r) 𝒪 →ₐ[𝒪] MvPowerSeries (Fin r) 𝒪) (hφ : ∀ i, φ (MvPowerSeries.X i) = f i) :
    ∃ (e : ℕ) (β : Fin e → MvPowerSeries (Fin r) 𝒪),
      (∀ x : MvPowerSeries (Fin r) 𝒪, ∃ c : Fin e → MvPowerSeries (Fin r) 𝒪, x = ∑ j, φ (c j) * β j) ∧
      (∀ c : Fin e → MvPowerSeries (Fin r) 𝒪, ∑ j, φ (c j) * β j = 0 → ∀ j, c j = 0) := by sorry
